\end{align*}
\]

We will eliminate \( y \) and \( z \) by manipulating these equations. First, let's multiply equation (1) by 3 and equation (2) by 4 to align the coefficients of \( y \):

\[
\begin{align*}
3(3x + 4y - 12z) &= 3(10), \\
